<h2 class="g-h2" id="scale">At scale</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>A span of up to 24 years shows years, up to 240 decades, beyond that centuries; the Date columns menu switches, and a width with more than 250 columns is offered disabled. The two scale previews below exercise axis, date and pan controls; count filtering needs a corresponding treatment list, shown in the first example. Long court names keep the tier column fixed while the matrix pans in its own frame, never the page.</p></div>
{% set ex = "citing-chart-century" %}{% set exTitle = "151 years of rows" %}{% include "guide/example.njk" %}
{% set ex = "citing-chart-dense" %}{% set exTitle = "64 courts" %}{% include "guide/example.njk" %}

<h2 class="g-h2" id="counting">Counting</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The counts come from <code>chartBreakdown</code> in <code>tools/chart-data.cjs</code>, an Eleventy filter:</p>
<p><code>{{ '{% set b = opinion.cited_by | chartBreakdown("cited-by", "severity", "citing_court_display", "citing_date_filed") %}' }}</code></p></div>
{{ table(["Rule", "Why"], [
  ["Every period from the first dated row to the last is a column, empty or not", "The scale stays honest: a gap of decades looks like a gap."],
  ["Rows without a valid date get their own column after the calendar", "\"Date not available\" is a fact about the data, not a year."],
  ["A row whose tier is not one of the five is left out and counted in <code>uncharted</code>", "An unfamiliar treatment label can't break the build; the coverage line says how many."],
  ["Ranges are inclusive, and each cell's label says so", "1900–1909 includes both years; narrowing matches exactly the counted rows."]
]) }}

<h2 class="g-h2" id="parameters">Parameters</h2>
{{ params([["b", "breakdown", "", "<code>chartBreakdown</code>'s result. <code>b.list</code> names the list it narrows: the cells link to <code>#&lt;list&gt;</code>, and only the list in the <code>[role=tabpanel]</code> whose <code>data-tab</code> matches reacts."]]) }}

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The matrix is a real <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> with a caption, row and column headers; zero cells read "0". Each count's label gives its tier, full range and number. The scroll region is focusable and named, with pan buttons for pointer users.</p></div>

